  "area": "3D geometry and texturing",
  "about": "Expected result-block values for the Paneveil rehearsal ROM and the release ROM's auto QA run, judged by tools/judge.py. Block layout: arm9/source/game/rehearsal.h. \"frame\" is the minimum number of frames to run, per boot. An item may name the captures it depends on (\"done\": the value index and bit mask that must be set) and whether it reads pixels (\"pixels\": a value above 0x7FFF is the ROM's \"not captured\" marker). \"known\" lists, per emulator version and renderer, the gating items expected to fail there; judge.py --profile passes only when the failing set matches exactly. Items of the kiln check carry \"done\" on flags bit 0: the check ran to the end and no GXSTAT wait timed out.",
  "block": {
    "address": "0x0237F000",
    "magic": 1380275779
  },
  "boots": {
    "rehearsal": {
      "rom": "paneveil-rehearsal.nds",
      "item_id": 1213355600,
      "item_id_text": "PVRH",
      "frames": 1200,
      "note": "the kiln check, the light box and a scripted play of the first window of every chapter; no save chip, no NitroFS"
    },
    "qa": {
      "rom": "paneveil.nds",
      "item_id": 1314013521,
      "item_id_text": "QARN",
      "frames": 4500,
      "note": "the release ROM's hidden auto QA mode (title: hold L+R+X+Y for 120 frames): every window played, the credits, then the kiln check and the light box once; the block uses the rehearsal's layout and adds the QA words at values[48..54] (verdict 1 PASS / 2 FAIL, log lines, SD flags, last state hash, checkpoints, lag, save flags)"
    }
  },
  "sources": {
    "GBATEK": "documented hardware behaviour; gating",
    "report:<ref>": "a hardware report by a third party (e.g. report:melonDS#2008); gating",
